        {"id": "s2", "text": "that several small vendors", "clickable": true, "isError": false},
        {"id": "s3", "text": "had to temporarily halt", "clickable": true, "isError": false},
        {"id": "s4", "text": "their operations.", "clickable": false}
      ],
      "explanation": "Topic: Advanced 'Such... that' Structures. No error. Inverting the sentence to 'Such was the impact... that...' is a correct and highly formal way to emphasize the degree of the impact."
    },
    {
      "id": "q42",
      "type": "multi_error",
      "question": "Click on error(s) and type correction.",
      "sentence": "The safety officer emphasized the strict protocols lest an accident occurs during the factory inspection.",
      "multiErrorSegments": [
        {"id": "s0", "text": "The safety officer emphasized", "clickable": false},
        {"id": "s1", "text": "the strict protocols", "clickable": true, "isError": false},
        {"id": "s2", "text": "lest an accident occurs", "clickable": true, "isError": true, "correctAnswers": ["lest an accident occur"]},
        {"id": "s3", "text": "during the factory inspection.", "clickable": false}
      ],
      "explanation": "Topic: 'Lest' Constructions. The conjunction 'lest' (meaning 'for fear that') is always followed by the subjunctive mood, which uses the base form of the verb ('occur'), not the third-person singular ('occurs')."
    },
    {
      "id": "q43",
      "type": "multi_error",
      "question": "Identify all errors (word, phrase, or clause).",
      "sentence": "If only I have invested in that property in South Jakarta five years ago, I would be financially secure now.",
      "multiErrorSegments": [
        {"id": "s0", "text": "If only I", "clickable": false},
        {"id": "s1", "text": "have invested", "clickable": true, "isError": true, "correctAnswers": ["had invested"]},
        {"id": "s2", "text": "in that property in South Jakarta", "clickable": true, "isError": false},
        {"id": "s3", "text": "five years ago,", "clickable": false},
        {"id": "s4", "text": "I would be financially secure now.", "clickable": true, "isError": false}
      ],
      "explanation": "Topic: 'If only' for Past Regrets. To express regret about a past situation, 'if only' must be followed by the past perfect tense ('had invested'), not the present perfect."
    },
    {
      "id": "q44",
      "type": "multi_error",
      "question": "Check for errors.",
      "sentence": "I would rather you did not disclose the confidential merger details to anyone outside the executive team.",
      "multiErrorSegments": [
        {"id": "s0", "text": "I would rather", "clickable": false},
        {"id": "s1", "text": "you did not disclose", "clickable": true, "isError": false},
