        {"id": "s3", "text": "relying on fossil fuels.", "clickable": true, "isError": false}
      ],
      "explanation": "Topic: 'Rather than' Parallelism. When 'rather than' is used to contrast two infinitive actions, the 'to' is typically omitted in the second part to maintain smooth parallelism ('to invest... rather than continue')."
    },
    {
